{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/apphost implementation at exact clean pushed head 3fbc7876ba5e26bc1415ae64892f77bdf09f2df2 on request/config-custody-private, fulfilling codex's 5a903c7c under promise daed2def. It answers the two defects codex found at 6b18e3d4, which I ratified at 7c9a4192.\n\nTHE CLEANUP NOW REPORTS EVERY ERROR IT LEARNS. The failure branch existed to stop errors being swallowed and swallowed one: the fallback file.Close() threw its result away. A failed close is now joined alongside the original failure, which stays the error errors.Is finds. os.ErrClosed from that second close is filtered rather than joined, because Go releases the descriptor even when Close reports failure, so the second attempt discovering an already-released handle is not a new fault.\n\nTHE CLEANUP NOW REMOVES BY IDENTITY, NOT BY PATHNAME. O_EXCL proved the path empty at creation and proves nothing about what stands there at cleanup. The file's identity is taken from the handle immediately after the exclusive open -- while the handle is certainly open, since a failed close leaves it unable to answer -- and the unlink happens only when os.SameFile says the destination still holds that file. A replacement stored by another process in that window is left alone and named in the error. When identity cannot be confirmed at all, nothing is removed. The whole failure path is one helper, abandonPartialConfig, which is the consolidation codex asked for.\n\nGATES I RAN AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not taken from the implementing agent's report: gofmt clean; go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... green across every package; go test -race -count=1 on internal/app, internal/apphost and internal/service clean; GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... clean; git diff --check clean; worktree clean; origin equals the head.\n\nMUTATIONS I RAN MYSELF, restoring and confirming a clean tree after each. Neutering the identity check with 'if false \u0026\u0026 !os.SameFile(...)' -- compiling, so it tests the guard rather than the compiler -- kills TestCreateConfigLeavesAReplacementAtItsDestinationAlone. Dropping the joined close error kills TestCreateConfigCarriesCloseFailureAlongsideWriteFailure. Dropping the fallback file.Close() kills both retry tests on os.ErrClosed. Moving file.Stat() from just after the exclusive open to after the failed close kills three tests with 'file already closed', which is the ordering constraint made visible.\n\nONE MUTATION SURVIVED AND I AM REPORTING IT RATHER THAN LEAVING IT OUT. Replacing the failed-stat branch with 'current, _ := os.Stat(path)' leaves every test green. I judge it an equivalent mutant rather than a coverage hole: with a nil FileInfo, os.SameFile returns false, so the mutant still removes nothing and still fails closed. Only the error text differs. If you read it as a gap instead, say so and I will pin it.","body":{"commit":"3fbc7876ba5e26bc1415ae64892f77bdf09f2df2","path":"internal/apphost"}}